The `stop` method in the `Progress` class was printing a blank line when `disabled=True` on non-interactive consoles. I added a check for `self.disable` in the `stop` method to make it symmetrical with the `start` method, ensuring no output is produced when the progress display is disabled.

```python
    def stop(self) -> None:
        """Stop the progress display."""
        if not self.disable:
            self.live.stop()
            if not self.console.is_interactive and not self.console.is_jupyter:
                self.console.print()
